        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3eafa396-f29e-5f39-a8b6-2a100346fab1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lowell George, Ian Hunter, Christopher Cross\n- Bands: Little Feat, Mott the Hoople\n- Songs and Albums: \"Ride Like the Wind\"\n- Roles: singer-songwriter, guitarist, vocalist, songwriter, record producer\n\nFacts:\n- Ian Hunter Patterson was born on 3 June 1939 and is known professionally as Ian Hunter.\n- Lowell Thomas George was born on April 13, 1945 and died on June 29, 1979.\n- Ian Hunter was the lead singer of the English rock band Mott the Hoople from its inception in 1969 to its dissolution in 1974.\n- Lowell George was an American songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, and record producer.\n- Lowell George was the primary guitarist, vocalist, and songwriter for the rock band Little Feat.\n- Christopher Cross dedicated \"Ride Like the Wind\" on the album's inner sleeve to Lowell George, formerly of Little Feat, after George died in 1979.\n- Ian Hunter participated as lead singer at Mott the Hoople's 2009 and 2013 reunions.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
